    "extracted text": "The paper studies Al–7Si–0.6Mg alloy F357 prepared from semi-solid metal (SSM) slurries using the CSIR-RCS process. Hardness measurements show that the primary α-Al has a hardness close to the macrohardness of the alloy (about 120 VHN at peak hardness). Various heat treatments were studied: solution treatment at 540°C for 1h followed by water quenching, natural aging (NA) at room temperature for 120h (T4 condition), and artificial aging at 180°C for up to 4h. The study focused on solute nanostructures formed during these treatments and their effect on strengthening.",
